    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554-a2">

                <pb facs="0559" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg525"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    735.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Duke of Tetuan to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In addition to my note of the 30th
                    of July last, relative to the proceedings followed in Cuba against the
                    naturalized American, Manuel Fernandez Chaqueilo, I have to inform your
                    excellency that the Captain-General of that island, in reply to the telegraphic
                    question made to him upon the subject, reports that the council of war sentenced
                    said Fernandez Chaqueilo to life imprisonment; but the auditor-general
                    dissented, and proposed that a death sentence should be imposed for having
                    belonged to an incendiary band. In view of that, and according to the provisions
                    for such cases in the Code of Military Justice, the cause shall be revised by
                    the supreme council of war and marine, to which it shall be sent by next
                    mail.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">The Duke of Tetuan.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
